wait [SimTalk]
The keyword wait interrupts the execution of the Method for the specified amount of simulation time. The
execution of the Method continues as soon as the time of the EventController advanced by the amount of
time you specified for the wait-statement.
Remarks
If a control is being executed during the reset phase and suspends itself with a wait instruction, Plant
Simulation deletes the suspension at the end of the reset phase.
A Method that is suspended by a wait instruction shows this in the tooltip in the Frame window.
@.move  -- the part exits
?.ExitLocked := true
wait 5  -- the exit is blocked for 5 seconds
?.ExitLocked := false
See also
Interrupting Method Execution with Wait
